<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hildegard of the Vinzgau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 758–783</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hildegard was a Frankish queen from the Alemannian nobility who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> around 771 and bore him nine children, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>. She was a patron of churches, including the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kempten">Kempten</a>, which honoured her as its benefactress. She died in 783 and was buried at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hildegard-of-the-vinzgau.jpg" alt="Hildegard of the Vinzgau" width="320" height="516" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Birk, Johannes; derivative work by Hic et nunc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hildegard_1499.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
